Conflicts: wine, wine64, wine32, wine-stable, wine-devel, wine-staging
Description: Windows programs on palOS, ready out of the box
 A ready-made Windows 11 environment: Wine 11 (with the Staging compatibility
 patches), .NET Framework programs (Wine Mono), the web engine Windows programs
 use for their own screens (Wine Gecko), and DirectX 8-12 through Vulkan (DXVK and
 vkd3d-proton) on graphics cards that have Vulkan. Nothing is downloaded the first
 time; each account gets its own copy in a few seconds.
 .
 Double-clicking an installer (.exe or .msi) runs it like on Windows; the installed
 program appears in Applications like any other app, and Utilities > Windows
 Programs removes it. Sound, graphics, the network, printers and the Documents,
 Desktop, Downloads, Music, Pictures and Videos folders are shared with palOS.
 .
 Not every Windows program runs under Wine: games with anti-cheat, software that
 installs Windows drivers and some copy-protected programs don't.
